{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-209454-r4587150","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Spiced Crème Caramel","sourcePageId":209454,"sourceRevision":"4587150","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:23:12Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Spiced%20Cr%C3%A8me%20Caramel&oldid=4587150","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:37.967Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for caramel","Category:Recipes for custard","Category:Recipes for pudding","Category:Recipes using bread","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using star anise","Category:Recipes using sweetened condensed milk","Category:Recipes using whole milk","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"dc089c145c1fe2f3cf1e6a4401d85e098ec4dd3040461f9d265668999869b26d","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Custard recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Caramel ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 1½ tbsp white granulated [[cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n\n=== Pudding ===\n* 750 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[cookbook:Milk|whole milk]]\n* 150 ml [[cookbook:Milk|sweetened condensed milk]]\n* 4 tbsp white granulated [[cookbook:sugar|sugar]]\n* 2 stars [[cookbook:Star Anise|star anise]]\n* 2 sticks [[cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 2–3 slices stale [[cookbook:Bread|white bread]]\n* 250 ml cold milk\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[cookbook:cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla essence]]\n* ½ cup room temperature milk\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Caramel ===\n# Heat the butter and sugar in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] over medium-high heat, stirring, until it caramelizes.\n# Cool caramel slightly, then transfer to a mold.\n# Let cool completely.\n\n=== Pudding ===\n# Bring the 750 ml milk, sweetened condensed milk, sugar, star anise, and the cinnamon sticks to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]], stirring occasionally.\n# Grind the bread in a [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]] until powdered. Add cold milk, and blend until smooth. Make sure there are no lumps.\n# Combine the cornstarch, vanilla, and ½ cup milk.\n# Stir the bread mixture and cornstarch mixture into the hot milk. [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]], stirring continuously, until the mixture becomes thick and smooth. Make sure it doesn't stick.\n# Remove from the heat, and pour into the mold over the cooled caramel.\n# Let cool to room temperature, then refrigerate for 3–4 hours.\n# Serve cold.\n\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for custard]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pudding]]\n[[Category:Recipes using star anise]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes for caramel]]\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sweetened condensed milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Ca